Reject crafted group descriptors and a zero mkfs block size

Backports, carried until lwext4 or the osvunikernel fork picks them up:

- gkostka/lwext4 PR #111, commit
  b9c842f168e6044bd03fe34e1237eda33c299908 (Chris Thomas): all of its
  library part, byte for byte (its tests are not carried).
  In ext4_fs.c it bounds the block and inode bitmap rebuild of an
  uninitialized group.  bit_max (from s_reserved_gdt_blocks and the GDT
  geometry) and inodes_per_group come straight from the superblock, so a
  crafted image drives ext4_bmap_bit_set() and the memset() past the end
  of the one-block bitmap buffer.  Each is now checked against
  block_size * 8 bits, and so are the bitmap, inode bitmap and inode
  table blocks marked in the group's own bitmap.  On error the bitmap
  block reference is released before returning EIO.  Fixes
  CVE-2025-71474 (ext4_fs_init_block_bitmap(), crafted
  s_reserved_gdt_blocks with BLOCK_UNINIT) and CVE-2025-71473
  (ext4_fs_init_inode_bitmap(), crafted s_inodes_per_group).
  In ext4_super.c it adds ext4_sb_check_geometry(), which refuses at
  mount, as Linux does, a superblock whose block or cluster size, blocks
  or inodes per group, inode size, group count, s_reserved_gdt_blocks
  (at most a quarter block of descriptor pointers) or s_first_meta_bg is
  out of range.  Images built for the two CVEs are therefore refused
  with ENOTSUP before any bitmap is rebuilt.  ext4_mount() and
  ext4_block_set_lb_size() now return an error instead of asserting on
  a block size the device cannot hold.
  0001's log_block_size > 6 check overlaps the new one; it stays, so
  0001 is unchanged.
- From the Aladdin-R-D/lwext4 fork (https://github.com/Aladdin-R-D/lwext4),
  1d32b2f17 (NULL dereference in ext4_dir_en_get_name_len): guard the
  directory entry pointer in this hot untrusted dir-read helper.
- From the same fork, fa299459e (division by zero in
  create_fs_aux_info): reject a zero block size before dividing by it in
  the mkfs path, with EINVAL rather than the fork's EFAULT.

Applies to osvunikernel/lwext4 6f6d8f7c509da696e71e80cc5a59abfc48e4971b
after 0001.

